---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Projects - Matt Hurley" 
  description="Independent software projects focused on education systems, privacy-first design, and practical problem-solving."
>
  <div class="container container-wide">
    <h1>Projects</h1>
    <p class="intro">
      Each project represents a deliberate response to real constraints, user needs, 
      and operational requirements. Architecture decisions are documented with context, 
      not abstracted into marketing language.
    </p>

    <div class="project-card">
      <img src="/sophia-logo.png" alt="Sophia STARS" class="project-logo">
      <h3>Sophia STARS</h3>
      <p class="project-meta">Internal Education Management System</p>
      <div class="tech-badges">
        <span class="tech-badge">Web Platform</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Role-Based Access</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Audit Trails</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Encrypted</span>
      </div>
      
      <p>
        A comprehensive student management and reporting system built for Sophia Mundi Steiner School. 
        Designed to replace fragmented workflows with a unified, privacy-first platform that serves 
        educators, leadership, and administrative staff.
      </p>

      <h4>The Problem</h4>
      <p>
        Schools often rely on disconnected tools—spreadsheets, paper forms, and generic software not 
        designed for their governance model. Sophia STARS consolidates student records, attendance, 
        assessments, incident tracking, and reporting into a single, purpose-built system.
      </p>

      <h4>Design Principles</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Privacy by Design</strong> — All student data is encrypted, access-controlled, and audited. No external services, no third-party analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Role-Based Access</strong> — Teachers see only their classes. Leadership has oversight. Parents have read-only access to their children's records.</li>
        <li><strong>Offline-First Mindset</strong> — Systems must remain functional during network issues. Data integrity is non-negotiable.</li>
        <li><strong>Audit Trails</strong> — Every change is logged with timestamp, user, and reason. Critical for governance and accountability.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Architecture</h4>
      <p>
        Hosted on internal infrastructure with strict access controls. Built using modern web technologies 
        optimized for reliability and maintainability. Data residency and sovereignty are core requirements.
      </p>

      <h4>Impact</h4>
      <p>
        Reduced administrative overhead, improved data accuracy, and provided leadership with real-time 
        insights into student progress and wellbeing. Teachers report significant time savings and 
        clearer communication pathways.
      </p>

      <div class="privacy-note">
        <strong>Privacy Notice:</strong> Sophia STARS is an internal system and is not publicly accessible. 
        No demos, screenshots of live data, or access credentials are available. This case study documents 
        the system's design and impact without compromising student privacy or data security.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card">
      <img src="/omencore-logo.png" alt="OmenCore" class="project-logo">
      <h3>OmenCore</h3>
      <p class="project-meta">Private Infrastructure Management Platform</p>
      <div class="tech-badges">
        <span class="tech-badge">Infrastructure</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Automation</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Monitoring</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">WireGuard</span>
      </div>
      
      <p>
        A unified control plane for managing personal and educational infrastructure—servers, 
        networking, backups, monitoring, and automation. Built to reduce operational complexity 
        and improve system reliability.
      </p>

      <h4>The Problem</h4>
      <p>
        Managing multiple servers, network devices, and services across different locations requires 
        consistent tooling and clear visibility. OmenCore consolidates these operations into a 
        single interface with strong security boundaries.
      </p>

      <h4>Key Features</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Centralized authentication and authorization</li>
        <li>Automated backup verification and rotation</li>
        <li>Network traffic monitoring and alerting</li>
        <li>Service health checks and incident response workflows</li>
        <li>Secure remote access via WireGuard VPN</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Design Decisions</h4>
      <p>
        Built with infrastructure-as-code principles. All configuration is version-controlled. 
        Deployments are repeatable and auditable. Security is layered—network isolation, 
        certificate pinning, and zero-trust access controls.
      </p>

      <h4>Learnings</h4>
      <p>
        Managing infrastructure is about predicting failure modes and building resilience. 
        Monitoring is not optional. Documentation is part of the system, not an afterthought.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        <a href="https://omencore.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit OmenCore Website →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card">
      <img src="/nbncomparelogo.PNG" alt="NBN Compare" class="project-logo">
      <h3>NBN Compare</h3>
      <p class="project-meta">Internet Service Provider Comparison Tool</p>
      <div class="tech-badges">
        <span class="tech-badge">Static Site</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">No Tracking</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Ad-Free</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Unbiased</span>
      </div>
      
      <p>
        A straightforward tool for comparing Australian NBN plans based on location, speed tier, 
        and actual costs. Built to cut through marketing noise and present factual comparisons.
      </p>

      <h4>The Problem</h4>
      <p>
        ISP comparison sites are often affiliate-driven, prioritizing commission over accuracy. 
        Users need clear, unbiased data to make informed decisions about their internet service.
      </p>

      <h4>Approach</h4>
      <p>
        No affiliate links. No sponsored placements. Just pricing data, speed tier information, 
        and contract terms. Users can filter by location (as NBN availability varies) and sort 
        by price, speed, or contract length.
      </p>

      <h4>Technical Details</h4>
      <p>
        Static site with client-side filtering. Data sourced directly from ISP websites and 
        updated regularly. No tracking, no analytics, no user data collected.
      </p>

      <h4>Impact</h4>
      <p>
        Provides a trusted reference point for those researching NBN plans without commercial bias.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        <a href="https://nbncompare.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit NBN Compare →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card">
      <img src="/bb-logo.png" alt="BrightBound Adventures" class="project-logo">
      <h3>BrightBound Adventures</h3>
      <p class="project-meta">Educational Game Platform</p>
      <div class="tech-badges">
        <span class="tech-badge">Flutter</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Cross-Platform</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Offline-First</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">ACARA Aligned</span>
      </div>
      
      <p>
        An offline-first, cross-platform educational app designed for children aged 4-12. 
        Built with Flutter to strengthen literacy and numeracy skills through engaging, 
        game-based learning aligned with ACARA v9.0 and NAPLAN standards.
      </p>

      <h4>The Problem</h4>
      <p>
        Many educational games prioritize engagement over learning outcomes, include ads and 
        tracking, or require constant internet connectivity. Teachers need tools that align 
        with curriculum standards, work offline, and provide meaningful progress tracking 
        without compromising student privacy.
      </p>

      <h4>Design Philosophy</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Offline-First</strong> — No internet connection required. Perfect for classrooms, travel, or areas with limited connectivity.</li>
        <li><strong>Child-Safe</strong> — Zero ads, no tracking, no accounts, no in-app purchases. Just pure learning.</li>
        <li><strong>Adaptive Difficulty</strong> — Content adjusts based on student performance to maintain appropriate challenge levels.</li>
        <li><strong>Curriculum-Aligned</strong> — Activities mapped to ACARA v9.0 and NAPLAN high-risk areas.</li>
        <li><strong>Privacy-Focused</strong> — All data stored locally on device. No cloud sync, no external services.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Learning Zones</h4>
      <p>
        Children explore five themed worlds: Word Woods (literacy), Number Nebula (numeracy), 
        Puzzle Peaks (logic), Story Springs (creative storytelling), and Adventure Arena 
        (coordination games). Each zone focuses on specific educational outcomes while 
        maintaining high engagement through gamification and avatar customization.
      </p>

      <h4>Technical Implementation</h4>
      <p>
        Built with Flutter for cross-platform compatibility (Android, iOS, and Web PWA). 
        Uses local Hive database for offline storage. Adaptive learning engine tracks skill 
        progression from LOCKED → INTRODUCED → PRACTISING → MASTERED. PIN-protected parent 
        dashboard provides progress analytics without compromising child privacy.
      </p>

      <h4>Outcomes</h4>
      <p>
        Currently in development with Phase 1 complete. The platform helps identify learning 
        gaps and provides students with self-paced practice opportunities. Teachers can monitor 
        progress without relying on external services or compromising student data.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        <a href="https://brightbound.matthurley.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit BrightBound Adventures →</a> | 
        <a href="https://github.com/theantipopau/brightbound_adventures" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on GitHub →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card">
      <h3>Windows Optimizers</h3>
      <p class="project-meta">System Optimization Scripts</p>
      <div class="tech-badges">
        <span class="tech-badge">PowerShell</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Open Source</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Performance</span>
        <span class="tech-badge">Documented</span>
      </div>
      
      <p>
        Two focused PowerShell scripts for optimizing Windows systems: one for touchscreen/tablet 
        devices, another for gaming rigs. Built to reduce bloat, improve performance, and remove 
        unnecessary services.
      </p>

      <h4>The Problem</h4>
      <p>
        Default Windows installations include services and features most users don't need, 
        consuming resources and creating maintenance overhead. Manual optimization is 
        time-consuming and error-prone.
      </p>

      <h4>Approach</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Touchscreen Optimizer</strong> — Improves responsiveness on tablets and convertibles by disabling unnecessary background tasks, optimizing power settings, and streamlining touch input handling.</li>
        <li><strong>Gaming Optimizer</strong> — Maximizes performance by disabling telemetry, stopping non-essential services, and optimizing network settings for low latency.</li>
      </ul>

      <h4>Technical Details</h4>
      <p>
        Scripts are idempotent and documented. Each change is explained with reasoning. 
        Users can review and modify scripts before execution. No telemetry, no remote execution.
      </p>

      <h4>Learnings</h4>
      <p>
        Windows optimization is about understanding tradeoffs. Every disabled service has 
        consequences. Documentation and user education are as important as the scripts themselves.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/theantipopau/windows11touchoptimizer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Touchscreen Optimizer on GitHub →</a> | 
        <a href="https://github.com/theantipopau/windows11nontouchgamingoptimizer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gaming Optimizer on GitHub →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
